{"author":{"id":"609bf866d4a5d716c19faf5d617b3bf3de478230d29602d72aad5aa90a80466f"},"ops":[{"type":3,"timestamp":1794553949,"nonce":"m8CcYWZEdWX7bEj2l9SlEJpL04Q=","message":"Fixed in 650afeb0 (local, not pushed). `expose_tls_base` now finds `__tls_base` as the global the name section calls `__tls_base`; else the only mutable i32 set by the start function or its direct callees that initialise passive data (memory.init or data.drop, i.e. `__wasm_init_memory`); else the start function's own body, as before. Only the start function and its direct callees are read, the other bodies are kept as references, so the cost for a large module is unchanged.\n\nChecked with hxn's two built modules, run with the rebuilt release ash, three times each:\n- counter-wasm (start function is `__wasm_init_memory`): PASS, unchanged.\n- counter-gen-wasm (start function `__wasm_start` calls `__wasm_apply_global_relocs` and `__wasm_init_memory`): was \"current thread handle already set during thread spawn\", now PASS 3 of 3.\n- the scratch probe (threads, thread::current before spawn, thread-local addresses): unchanged.\nUnit tests added in ash_wasm_link: a wrapper start function with a GOT global set beside the real one finds the right global; a start function that sets two candidates is left alone without a name section and resolved with one. ash_wasm_link and ash_wasm_runtime tests and clippy pass, including the browser target's.\n\nNot checked: the browser host. It calls the same function (browser/dylink.rs), so it gets the same detection, but nothing was run in a page.\n\nLimit seen on the way, not changed: the export is added only when the module already has an export section; a side module with none has no primitives to call.","files":null}]}